- Both the Pod and its container are running, but the container is not Ready.
- 0/1 — The container isn't ready to receive normal Service traffic.
- Running — The container is still running.
- 0 restarts — Kubernetes hasn't restarted the container.

- The kube-probe/1.34 user-agent in the access logs confirms the request came from Kubernetes' probe mechanism.
- This demonstrates that a readiness failure doesn't restart the container. Kubernetes keeps checking the endpoint and can mark the Pod ready again if the probe succeeds.
- Your events show x63 over 9m14s. That means Kubernetes recorded repeated probe failures over that period. Unlike liveness probes, readiness probes do not restart the container after repeated failures.

